- **Framework.** Emit CUDA C directly from the current Tix IR. The existing transformation contract and async differential checker handle GPU batching and evidence reuse. The local probe verified both, so the design proposes zero framework changes.
- **Remote tool.** Separate runtime inputs from the compile key, isolate each invocation’s working directory, and check the compiler and driver identity before reusing evidence.
- **Numerical relation.** Use sampled tolerance against the current revision’s f64 result, with an f32 guard. On the GB10, `expf`, `logf`, and `tanhf` differed from Node f32 in 19,892, 2,148, and 2,447 of 65,536 trials each. An ordered sum matched the interpreter bit for bit yet used 2.93 times the fixed f64 allowance. The proposed tolerance covered the tested folds. [GB10 observations](/home/manuel/code/wesen/2026-11-24--compiler-workbench/.claude/worktrees/t2-sx-irwb-022-b/ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-B--lowering-tix-to-cuda-checked-on-the-gpu-machine/scripts/01-gb10-probe/observed.json)

Implementation and the six corpus timings follow the design review.
